WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.740
- But you were on stage actually,

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.410
and this is more of a serious thing,

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.950
but actually I had friends
at the Vegas shooting.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.820
They were Brian, and actually
Brandon's best friend,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.660
my husband's best friend.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.130
He and his wife were there,
at the Vegas shooting when

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.320
it happened when you were
doing your show and everything.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.210
And I just, I know you just
did a show in Vegas recently,

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.900
like, to kind of I don't know, I guess

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.780
what was the point of you doing that?

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.658
Because I, right when that happened,

00:00:24.658 --> 00:00:27.840
our friends were literally
texting us during the shooting.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.189
And we were like 'what?'

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:32.980
And it terrified me, to ever go on stage.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.040
And I've been on stage forever.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:35.873
- Yeah.

00:00:35.873 --> 00:00:37.130
- But it just scares you,
because you're so vulnerable.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.440
- Yeah, I mean it's, you know,

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.448
obviously something that I
wouldn't wish on anybody.

00:00:41.448 --> 00:00:44.310
And you know, I think for us,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.210
going back to Vegas was something that

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.010
I think we wanted to do it the right way.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.730
We didn't want to go in
trying to do it too soon.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.630
And we felt like there was going to be

00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:56.120
a lot of people at our show that probably

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.880
haven't been to one of our
shows, maybe you haven't

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.890
been to a concert at all since that show.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.710
And if they were going to come back out,

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.270
you know that was part of
the healing process for them.

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:08.250
You know, we wanted to make
it a safer environment.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.760
Something that made them feel safer.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:10.593
- Yeah.

00:01:10.593 --> 00:01:12.543
- So we did Park MGM,

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.770
and so a little five thousand seat arena,

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.310
that you know, the other one was outside,

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.215
thirty, forty thousand
people, whatever it was.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.048
- Yeah.

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:24.550
- And so this was a little smaller,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.350
little more intimate
where people could come,

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.667
hopefully feel a little more at ease.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:29.520
- Yeah.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.380
- Hopefully it helps some of them.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.900
I mean, we had to kind of
get on stage the next week,

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:33.733
you know.

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:35.683
And start trying to get
through all that, so.

00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:37.540
- How did you do that, right off the bat?

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:38.760
Did you talk to anyone?

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.060
Because I'm telling you what-

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.790
- You know the best thing that-

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:42.838
- Especially having kids.

00:01:42.838 --> 00:01:43.671
- Yeah.

00:01:43.671 --> 00:01:44.517
- You know what I'm saying?

00:01:44.517 --> 00:01:45.830
Like it's not just you going
out there, you have a family.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.530
- Ya, it's, I mean, it was rough.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.980
I think the best thing
that could have happened,

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:49.820
was the fact,

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.250
not that could have happened,
but the best thing for me,

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.880
was the fact that my wife
was there, went through it,

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.740
my band was there, went
through it, my crew, everybody.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.390
And so we kind of leaned on each other.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.360
You know, for that stuff.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.010
Kind of talked through it,
nobody kept it bottled up,

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.860
and if you had a breakdown,

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.340
you kind of had it in front of everybody

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.760
and everybody knew what was going on.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.958
- Yeah.

00:02:08.958 --> 00:02:11.280
- You know, my wife, we
could talk and she understood

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.210
what was going on, because she was there.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.043
- Yeah.

00:02:14.043 --> 00:02:15.250
- You know, and so it was, I think to me,

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.950
that probably helped more than anything.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.224
But you know, were on the
other side of it now and

00:02:19.224 --> 00:02:21.770
we're part of a group, not
only one family anymore.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:23.008
- Yeah.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:23.841
- So it's a cool group.

00:02:23.841 --> 00:02:24.771
- It is, it is. It's a good thing.

00:02:24.771 --> 00:02:25.604
(applause)

